@*
    Site wide atmosphere, in two halves.

    BACK (behind the page content, z-index 0)
        grid-lines  faint architectural grid, gives the black some structure
        haze        two huge slow drifting colour blooms
        sweep       a wide soft light band that crosses the page now and then

    FRONT (over everything, z-index 100)
        scanlines   faint horizontal banding
        grain       animated film grain
        vignette    darkened edges

    The split matters: anything translucent on the page (cards, panels, the
    nav bar) now shows the grid and haze through it, while the film effects
    still coat the whole screen including those panels. One single layer
    could not do both.

    Everything ignores pointer events, and no images are downloaded: the
    grain is an inline SVG turbulence filter encoded as a data URL.
*@

<div class="atmo-back" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="grid-lines"></div>
    <div class="haze haze-warm"></div>
    <div class="haze haze-cold"></div>
    <div class="sweep"></div>
</div>

<div class="atmo-front" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="scanlines"></div>
    <div class="grain"></div>
    <div class="vignette"></div>
</div>
